Title: Pass winwrap's architecture define to MASM
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

  src\forwarders_x86.asm(26): error A2052: forced error : neither WINWRAP_X86
  nor WINWRAP_X64 is defined; the build is not passing the architecture define
  to ml [.../deps/winwrap/winwrap.vcxproj]

  ml.exe /c /nologo /Zi /Fo"...forwarders_x86.obj" /W3 /errorReport:prompt
         /Tasrc\forwarders_x86.asm

No /D on that command line. winwrap's redirect table is written twice --
static_redirects.cc for Clang, forwarders_{x86,x64}.asm for MSVC -- and the
MASM pair guards its whole body on WINWRAP_X86 or WINWRAP_X64, because both
files have to be in the source list: one generated project holds every
configuration at once and a source cannot be chosen per architecture. Without
the define both assemble to nothing, winwrap exports no slots, and node.exe
fails at the final link on the anchor it names in /INCLUDE:.

winwrap.gyp does declare the define. It puts it on abstract configurations
called x86_Base and x64_Base, which take effect only in a tree whose own
configurations inherit_from those names -- sawbuck-ng's do. Node's are plain
Debug and Release with no inherit_from anywhere, so those configurations are
never instantiated and the setting quietly never applies.

Delivering it from target_defaults works instead, for two reasons that do not
hold for every consumer but do hold here. target_defaults reaches every target
in the build including winwrap's own, which is visible in the generated
winwrap.vcxproj: it already carries Node's defines, NODE_OPENSSL_CONF_NAME
among them. And one Node generation covers exactly one architecture, so
target_arch is unambiguous -- which is precisely the assumption winwrap.gyp
cannot make, hence its abstract configurations.

Added to the *second* 'conditions' key in target_defaults, not the first.
There are two, a .gypi is a Python literal, and the later key silently
replaces the earlier -- so the error_on_warn block in the first one is already
dead, and anything else put there would be too. This is the same trap that
cost 07-winwrap-xp-link.patch a round.

Needs 12-gyp-masm-settings.patch to be in place, or gyp drops MASM settings
during the MSVS-to-MSBuild conversion with nothing but a warning.

diff --git a/common.gypi b/common.gypi
--- a/common.gypi
+++ b/common.gypi
@@ -441,6 +441,41 @@
     'msvs_cygwin_shell': 0, # prevent actions from trying to use cygwin
 
     'conditions': [
+      # winwrap's MASM forwarders guard their whole body on an architecture
+      # define, and both files are in its source list because one generated
+      # project holds every configuration at once. Without the define both
+      # assemble to nothing, winwrap exports no redirect slots, and node.exe
+      # fails at the final link on the anchor it names in /INCLUDE:.
+      #
+      # winwrap.gyp does declare this, on abstract configurations named
+      # x86_Base and x64_Base, which only take effect in a tree whose own
+      # configurations inherit_from those names. Node's are plain Debug and
+      # Release, so nothing instantiates them and the setting never applies.
+      # Delivering it here works instead because target_defaults reaches every
+      # target in the build, winwrap's included, and because one Node
+      # generation covers exactly one architecture, so target_arch is
+      # unambiguous.
+      #
+      # This list and not the one earlier in target_defaults: there are two
+      # 'conditions' keys in this dict, a .gypi is a Python literal, and the
+      # later key silently replaces the earlier. Anything added to the first
+      # is discarded without a word.
+      #
+      # Needs 12-gyp-masm-settings.patch, or gyp drops MASM settings silently.
+      [ 'OS=="win" and target_arch=="ia32"', {
+        'msvs_settings': {
+          'MASM': {
+            'PreprocessorDefinitions': ['WINWRAP_X86=1'],
+          },
+        },
+      }],
+      [ 'OS=="win" and target_arch=="x64"', {
+        'msvs_settings': {
+          'MASM': {
+            'PreprocessorDefinitions': ['WINWRAP_X64=1'],
+          },
+        },
+      }],
       [ 'configuring_node', {
         'msvs_configuration_attributes': {
           'OutputDirectory': '<(DEPTH)/out/$(Configuration)/',
